course: dictionary
lesson: 15257
title: Shredded: torn or cut into thin strips
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Shredded» comes from the verb shred, which means to tear or cut something into thin strips or small pieces. Read the words around it to find the meaning. «The storm shredded the sail into long ribbons» tells you the storm tore the sail into pieces.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? In «She shredded the carrots for the salad», a cook cuts carrots into thin strips. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word: "She cut the carrots into thin strips for the salad" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Shredded can also describe something already cut up, like «shredded cheese» on a pizza. Here it is an adjective, a word that tells you about a thing. Shred is the action; shredded can be the action in the past or a description of the food.
fact: Shred means to tear or cut something into thin strips or small pieces.
fact: «Shredded» means torn or cut into thin strips or small pieces.
fact: In cooking, «shredded» lettuce, carrot or cheese has been cut or grated into thin strips.
fact: Paper that is shredded has been cut up by a machine so no one can read it. Shredding old letters with names and bank details helps stop identity theft.
fact: Slang: «shredded» can mean having very visible muscles, or playing a guitar or skateboarding brilliantly. Slang is informal, so use it only in casual talk.
exercise: «She shredded the carrots into thin strips for the salad.» What does shredded mean here? | Put in a box | *Cut into thin strips | Cooked whole in a pan | Washed and dried
exercise: «The machine shredded the old letters so nobody could read them.» Why were the letters shredded? | To send them to a friend | *So nobody could read them | To keep them for a museum | To make them smell nice
exercise: «Put some shredded cheese on the pizza.» Find and copy one word that means cut into thin pieces. | the | pizza | *shredded | cheese
test: «The storm shredded the sail into long ribbons.» What does shredded mean? | Painted bright blue | Washed clean | Folded neatly | *Torn into pieces
test: Which of these is a shredded food? | A glass of milk | A whole apple | *A bag of shredded lettuce | A loaf of bread
exam: Why do people shred old letters that have their name and bank details on them? | To make them into a cereal | *To stop identity theft | To cook them into a meal | To give them as a present
